      "id": 15976,
      "name": "robb8888",
      "username": "robb8888",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-12-20T05:50:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I was giving the new heroes a test drive (iOS version), and had all four of them (KNYFE, Naturalist, Sentinels, Parse) playing against Omnitron in the Wagner Mars Base. &nbsp;Naturalist was in his Gazelle form, so I played Hyperactive Senses, the text of which states:<br>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\"Reveal the top 2 cards of any 2 decks, &nbsp;Put them back on top of their decks in any order. &nbsp; [And if in Gazelle Form]: You may discard the top card of any 2 decks.\" &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The game first gave me the option to select a deck from which to reveal cards (I selected Parse), then another deck from which to reveal cards (I selected the environment). &nbsp;The game revealed the top two cards on each deck, then allowed me to rearrange them, per the card text. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here's where the bug/possible rules interpretation comes into play. &nbsp;Reading the card, it says \"<span>[And if in Gazelle Form]: You may discard the top card of any 2 decks.\" &nbsp;Going with the traditional interpretation of cards that say \"may,\" I took that to mean that I could discard the top card of (a) two different decks, (b) only one deck, or (c) no decks at all. &nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>I went with choice (b) -- I wanted to discard the top card of the environment deck, but no others. &nbsp;However, once I had discarded the top deck of the environment deck, the game forced me to discard another top card; it didn't give me an option to skip the second. &nbsp;Not only that, but it made me discard a card from a different deck, even though the card does not say \"....discard the top card of any 2 *DIFFERENT* decks,\" or \"discard the top card from one deck, then another deck.\" &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>Is this a bug, or a rules interpretation? &nbsp;Is the \"Gazelle Form\" choice on the card an either/or -- either you discard two cards or none at all? &nbsp;If so, is that on purpose, or is it something that maybe/could/should be tweaked in a future edit?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
